Falsifies `pci::verification::read_bars_is_total_for_any_device`.

The defect: the BAR loop runs one slot past the end, `0..=slots` in place of `0..slots`. An
endpoint has six BARs and both spellings look like "all of them" at a glance; the flag that skips a
64-bit BAR's upper half already makes the slot bookkeeping here non-obvious.

Expected to fail: the totality claim, as an out-of-bounds index on `out[i]` at `i == 6`. It
needs a device that reports an endpoint header and answers the size probe with a usable mask on
the seventh slot, which is exactly the arbitrary-response regime this harness quantifies over and
nothing a fixture supplies.

diff --git a/crates/pci/src/lib.rs b/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
--- a/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/pci/src/lib.rs
@@ -435,7 +435,7 @@ pub fn read_bars(
     // Set when the slot before was the lower half of a 64-bit BAR, whose upper half this slot is.
     // A flag rather than a two-slot step, so the loop is bounded by its range alone.
     let mut upper_half = false;
-    for i in 0..slots {
+    for i in 0..=slots {
         if core::mem::take(&mut upper_half) {
             continue;
         }
